//
// For people, on sites with a model configured. Someone with no login can ask on a site that allows it (askForVisitors in the site settings). Agents should use their own model, with the tools the API already has. Being over the limit is an ordinary error. Otherwise the answer is server-sent events with JSON in each data line, and type says which: step (what is being looked up), sources (pages it can cite, each with a number), text (a piece of the answer), restart (what was said so far is not part of the answer), then done or error. done has the final text, in which [1] refers to citations, the id to rate it with if questions are being kept, and answered, which is whether it could point at a page.
